## Weekly check-ins

To keep an overview of the current status of active tasks, team leads will write a **weekly check-in every weekend, usually on Saturday.** Here's an example for a check-in:

> Hey team, here's the weekly check-in
> 
> @MalicousEasterBunny123 - Was doing some research. [Iwatodai Streets environment model](https://github.com/orgs/p3d-project/projects/1/views/1?filterQuery=label%3A%22%F0%9F%A7%8A+3d%22&pane=issue&itemId=208482391&issue=p3d-project%7Cpersona-3-dual%7C303). Still WIP. How's progress/any plans on what you will do?
> 
> @HappyHamster - Was doing some research. [Makoto character model](https://github.com/orgs/p3d-project/projects/1/views/1?filterQuery=label%3A%22%F0%9F%A7%8A+3d%22&pane=issue&itemId=208482391&issue=p3d-project%7Cpersona-3-dual%7C303) & [Iwatodai Dorm (lounge) environment model](https://github.com/orgs/p3d-project/projects/1/views/1?filterQuery=label%3A%22%F0%9F%A7%8A+3d%22&pane=issue&itemId=208482787&issue=p3d-project%7Cpersona-3-dual%7C304). Still WIP. How's progress/any plans on what you will do?
> 
> ...
> 
> All 3D issues are [here](https://github.com/orgs/p3d-project/projects/1/views/1?filterQuery=label%3A%22%F0%9F%A7%8A+3d%22)
> 
> If you're working on something but I've missed it, leave a message below.

This is to ensure no one gets stuck on a task, that the GitHub project board stays up to date, checking the current availability of individual team members and clarifying uncertainties on current tasks.

## Applicant Management

People who add themselves to the Applicant role will immediately get pinged in a private thread under the #apply-to-the-team channel. Team leads will also be pinged! The private thread simply contains application instructions and is where applicants will be notified of their application status, and can privately talk to team leads. Applicants will apply to the team using the Google Form (contained in the instructions) & team leads can view applications via the linked Google Sheet.

Instead of pinging/DM'ing applicants regarding their application status, use Elizabeth bot within the applicant's private thread`/approve [user] [role1] [optional: role2]`

`/reject [user] [optional: role1] [optional: role2]`

For /reject in particular, if you don't specify any roles, then it auto-defaults to rejecting from ALL roles!

Note that:

- Team leads don't give a reason, they just say approve/rejected
- Team leads don't give feedback on application results (even if people ask)

Once team leads have approved/rejected an applicant & the applicant has seen the message (or they don't respond within 48hrs), then in the private thread, "end" the application process via `/close_ticket [user]` & delete the applicant's application info in the Google Sheet.

## Documentation

Team leads are responsible for relevant documentation pertaining to your team on both the Google Drive (Google Doc files) & on docs.p3dual.com.

### Google Docs

Editing the Google Docs is self-explanatory. Simply find the doc file in the Google Drive, and start editing!

### docs.p3dual.com

To edit docs on docs.p3dual.com,

1. Go to [docs.p3dual.com/keystatic](https://docs.p3dual.com/keystatic) & sign in with your GitHub account
1. Create a new branch with the docs/ prefix

![](@assets/docs/images/team-lead/image.png)

You can now select documentation files & edit them! Ensure that once changes have been made to a page, the **"Save" button in the top right corner is clicked**!

![](@assets/docs/images/team-lead/image.png)

The docs website uses markdown (.md) formatting. The docs website also has custom components that you can access by clicking the + icon in the text editor.

![custom-components](@assets/docs/images/team-lead/custom-components.png)

To create a new page on the docs website, simply click "Add" in the top right corner of the page.

![add-page](@assets/docs/images/team-lead/add-page.png)
